            "subject": "LU-9 lod: weighted round-robin QoS allocation"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-06 00:36:22.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-06 00:36:22.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-19823 lod: spread failover groups over the RR array",
        "message": "LU-19823 lod: spread failover groups over the RR array\n\nWithout failure domains, the round-robin array only keeps the targets\nof each server apart.  The targets of the two servers of an HA pair\ncan still be next to each other in the array, so consecutive stripes\nof a file are on servers that can fail together, or be unavailable\ntogether while one of them fails over to the other.\n\nWhen no target has a failure domain, ltd_rr_failover_order() groups\nthe targets by the lowest NID of their primary and failover\nconnections, which is the same for all the targets that can fail over\nto each other, and orders the array by group as for failure domains.\nThe groups are ranked by NID, first by network and then by address,\nand lu_rr_group_order() orders them by the reversed bits of their\nrank, so groups with close NIDs, likely in the same network or rack,\nare mostly far apart in the array.  Unlike failure domains, this only\norders the array, and does not limit where the stripes of a layout or\nits mirrors may go.  The failover NIDs are read from the import at\neach rebuild of the array, so add_conn and del_conn take effect at the\nnext rebuild.\n\nAdd a -F option to lod_rr_test to put the OSSs in HA pairs, and check\nthat consecutive OSTs in the array are on different pairs.  Without\nthe ordering, \"lod_rr_test -f -o 4-64 -s 2-16 -F\" finds OSTs of one HA\npair next to each other in 1852 of 30512 combinations, and in none\nwith it.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5.5 ltvm,llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I39eae90881b61feee2e9b2aa20978a38e93ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
